Original commit body from c90c135c33b5145a6445ae7da8326721ab065e85:

The js_module linker sent every bare specifier no alias or workspace
package resolved to the npm route, so require('fs') minted
javascript:npm:0-0:fs:package -- kind package, package_ecosystem npm,
tier 3 "npm_package (third-party dependency)". 540 of the 2,771
package-node resolutions the WI-halol shape-5 audit enumerated were the
runtime's own modules (path 127, fs 95, http 67, child_process 38, util 36,
assert 36, os 23, url 21 ...) claimed as dependencies. js_ts already had
the core-module list; the linker did not read it.

* The list moves to js_package_entry as NODE_CORE_MODULES with
  is_node_core_module (`fs`, `fs/promises`, any `node:` specifier; not
  `fs-extra`). js_ts's private copy is deleted and it reads the shared one,
  so the two cannot drift.
* The linker skips the npm route for a core module: no package node, and
  the import stays the analyzer's external stand-in (whose missing stdlib
  ecosystem label is WI-hotut's, unchanged).

The deleted copy moves js_ts.py's lines, so three line-pinned citations
relocate by anchor (module_key_axis 7835 -> 7823, 1370 -> 1358;
signature_axis 6575 -> 6563).

Measured, survey before (dev caa332e01c) and after: pm2 package nodes 77 ->
55 (22 core modules, 301 import edges), knex 60 -> 48 (12, 119 edges) --
the audit's per-repo counts exactly; no non-core package node lost, none
added.

Tests: test_js_core_modules_not_npm.py through run_behavior_map (fs, path,
fs/promises, node:child_process get no package node; lodash and fs-extra
keep theirs); is_node_core_module in test_js_module_linker.py. Two
mutations (linker ignores the list, no subpath split) each turn a test red.

Addresses WI-tufob; unblocks WI-halol's shape-5 grant.

